The screen shows number forty-two.
I walk over to a counter.
A woman smiles and welcomes me.
She asks for my details.
"My name is Maya," I say.
"I am thirty-one years old."
"And I come from Mexico."
She nods kindly.
I give her my passport and my papers.
My new address is on the papers.
It is house number seven.
She looks at my papers and types on the computer.
Everything is in order.
